{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch8HfEvQrhHPYnGXQAYKH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Review of `tail`\n\n**Capabilities held.** `tail(dir: &Fs, n: usize)` takes the same `&Fs` that `read_all` already takes. It gets no new capability and doesn't hold one beyond its call: it has no struct fields and doesn't clone or store `dir`.\n\n**What it does with `Fs`.**\n- It only calls `dir.read_to_string(name)` (line 64).\n- It reads only `current.log`, `old.1.log` and `old.2.log`, the same three files `read_all` reads.\n- It makes no writes, renames, `open_with`, or directory listing, so it never writes where it used to read.\n- It goes from newest to oldest and stops once it has `n` lines, as the description says.\n- A `NotFound` error skips the file and any other error is returned, matching `read_all` and the description.\n\n**Other authority.**\n- It makes no `print!`, `println!`, `eprint!` or `eprintln!` calls, so nothing goes to the output sinks.\n- It touches no `Net`, `Clock`, `Rand`, `Env`, `Stdin`, `Proc` or `Tasks`.\n- The data goes only to the caller, as the return value.\n\n**Public surface.** `tail` is a new public function that takes an `Fs`, but the description asks for exactly this function. Its reach is no wider than the existing public `read_all`.\n\n**Other changes.** None. `RotLog` and `read_all` are unchanged.\n\nThe change takes no authority beyond what the description calls for.\n\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"approve\", \"findings\": []}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":338,"cache_read_input_tokens":4734,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":338},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"s